    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 🔄 Automated n8n Workflow Backup to GitHub\n\nThis workflow automatically backs up every workflow on your n8n instance to a GitHub repository on a 12-hour schedule. It is smart about what it commits — it only pushes a file when the actual workflow logic has changed, ignoring noise like position shifts, credential IDs, or metadata updates that don't affect how a workflow runs.\n\n### How it works\n1. A Schedule Trigger fires every 12 hours and sets the target GitHub folder path via the Input node.\n2. It lists all existing files in the GitHub backup folder to know what has already been saved.\n3. It retrieves all workflows from the n8n API, converts each one to a formatted JSON file, and encodes it in base64 for GitHub upload.\n4. For each workflow, it generates a filename from the workflow name and first tag (slugified), plus a timestamped commit message.\n5. A check determines whether the file already exists in the repo:\n   - **New file** → uploaded directly to GitHub.\n   - **Existing file** → the remote file is fetched and its content is compared against the current workflow using a deep diff. Volatile fields (IDs, positions, credentials, metadata) are stripped before comparison so only meaningful logic changes trigger a commit. If changes are detected, the file is updated; if not, the workflow is skipped entirely.\n\n### Setup\n1. **n8n API credential** — create an n8n API key and connect it to the `Retrieve workflows` node.\n2. **GitHub API credential** — connect a GitHub personal access token to all GitHub nodes.\n3. **Repository** — create a GitHub repo to store the backups (currently set to `self-hosted-n8n-backup`).\n4. **Folder path** — update the `Input` node with the folder name you want files saved under (currently `oracle-arm-n8n`).\n5. **Author details** — update the author name and email in the `Upload file` node to match your GitHub account.\n\n### Customization tips\n- Change the schedule interval in the trigger node (currently every 12 hours).\n- Add more folder paths by duplicating the Input node and branching the trigger if you manage multiple n8n instances.\n- Extend the `deepClean` function in the Code node to strip or preserve additional fields based on your comparison needs.",
        "height": 928,
        "width": 672
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
